cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use First Edition, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "First Edition: a zero-build publishing platform for student newspapers"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-10-18
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ariel-378/First-Edition"
url: "https://ariel-378.github.io/First-Edition/"
abstract: >-
  A free, open-source website and editor dashboard for student newspapers, written in
  plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript with no build step, no framework and no runtime
  dependencies. It runs on GitHub Pages or inside a school's existing website platform,
  which supplies sign-in and decides who is an editor. Every published story is also
  emitted as a static page so links preview in group chats; a WordPress or SNO archive
  imports in one command; 1,093 automated checks in 25 jsdom suites drive the real pages.
keywords:
  - student journalism
  - scholastic press
  - static web publishing
  - zero-dependency software
  - content management
  - GitHub Pages
  - web accessibility
authors:
